    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters August 4th with a clear hierarchy at the top of the order, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** and **Mickey Moniak**. **Corbin Carroll** is our premier start at an 87.14 efficiency score; he benefits immensely from facing V\u00e1squez, who struggles with a 4.92 xERA, allowing **Corbin Carroll** to leverage his elite speed against a soft target. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) is a must-start, as he enjoys a massive 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup against Peralta. **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.13) also stands out as a strong play; his ability to capitalize on Singer\u2019s 4.40 xERA combined with a solid lineup spot in the three-hole makes him a cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive floor.\n\nOn the bench, **Travis Bazzana** was the closest to cracking the lineup but ultimately fell short with a score of 37.71. Despite decent base projections, the combination of a difficult L/L platoon matchup against Manaea and a restrictive internal floor of 40.0 effectively benched him in favor of higher-ceiling options. Meanwhile, we are monitoring a significant 44% rain risk for **Austin Riley**. While his 58.16 score is respectable and bolstered by favorable SP delivery times that aid his situational utility, the weather remains a volatility factor. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **Cole Young**, whose 46.56 score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite-hold pitcher (50% SB suppression rate), forcing us to lean heavily on the speed upside of our top-tier outfielders to carry the category load.",
